Z||000000||Haze_Performance||07-13-2001||01:32 AM||||I'm contemplating going with coil overs. <A HREF="http://www.shelbycustom.com/addons/addons.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.shelbycustom.com/addons/addons.html</A> <P>Anyone here anything about this company?<P>Thanks<BR><I>Haze</I>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.ws6fiero.com" TARGET=_blank><BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/classicfieroowners3.gif">    </A><BR><FONT SIZE="1"><FONT COLOR="blue"><B>Click above to visit my website.</B></FONT></FONT>||||reg||10
Z||000001||chester||07-13-2001||07:52 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Haze_Performance:<BR><B>I'm contemplating going with coil overs. <A HREF="http://www.shelbycustom.com/addons/addons.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.shelbycustom.com/addons/addons.html</A> <P>Anyone here anything about this company?<P>Thanks<BR><I>Haze</I>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I personally don't know about this company but by looking at the setup it looks to me like you have to modify the front cross member to use their coilover setup.  You might want to ask them before hand.  The reason that I mention this is because I have coil overs on all corners of my car (RCC) and the guy before me modified the design and went with a bracket to mount the top of the coil over to the frame (simular to what I see on this setup. He wanted to drop the car 2" and this accomplished that).  What happens is you have to cut the stock spring perchs off the cross member.  This weakens the cross member.  Both of my upper control arms literally ripped off the cross member because of this mod.  RCC's design uses the stock spring perches to mount the coilover.  They have a custom hat that bolts to the coil over and then sits in the cross member spring perch and gets bolted into place.  I finally got my replacement parts to fix it right. Just thought that I would pass my experience along and try to save you some grief.  If your interested in the RCC setup let me know and I'll e-mail you their contact info.  They are cheaper thru them also ($395 I think) and they use carrera shocks.<P>Rob D.<P><BR>Rob D.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigline.jpg">   <BR>Modified 2.8<BR>2.5" Drop<BR>11" Brakes<BR>17" Revolutions<BR>RCC Coilover Suspension||||reg||1
Z||000002||gt2437||07-13-2001||05:08 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by chester:<BR><B> If your interested in the RCC setup let me know and I'll e-mail you their contact info.  They are cheaper thru them also ($395 I think) and they use carrera shocks.<P>Rob D.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hi Rob,<BR>I'm interested in RCC's coilovers, see my post Frame Flex - who's got it?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">   TIA<P>||||reg||1
